# Hash-pinned Discovery inputs must be byte-identical in every working tree.
#
# The V4/V4.1 pipeline records `sha256_file(<source map>)` in its acquisition
# and reference manifests, and every consuming stage re-verifies it. This repo
# has no other .gitattributes and the owner's git runs `core.autocrlf=true`, so
# a Windows checkout rewrote scripts/discovery_v4_sources.json to CRLF while git
# stored LF -- the file hashed ba3f413a... in the tree against the 6f21efcd...
# the V4 build pinned, and `discovery_v4_build_reference.py` would have refused
# its own inputs with "acquisition manifest source-map hash mismatch".
#
# Keep these two paths LF-only. Do NOT widen this to the whole tree: that would
# renormalize thousands of unrelated files.
scripts/discovery_v4_sources.json text eol=lf
scripts/discovery_v4_1_sources.json text eol=lf
scripts/discovery_v4_2_sources.json text eol=lf
scripts/discovery_v4_2_public_first_identities.json text eol=lf
